WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.350
Start from what the guide and
Microsoft Learn already give you.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.917
Create the custom roles in Defender's
unified role-based access control,

3
00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:11.875
in four permission groups, assigned
to groups and data sources.

4
00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:15.900
Activate it per workload, which needs
at least Security Administrator.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.405
Connect the read path with Connect
M G Graph, the Global environment,

6
00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:24.588
and two scopes: security incident
read, and threat hunting read.

7
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:26.691
Then validate with Learn's own call:

8
00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:29.737
list up to five incidents
with no permission error.

9
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:34.901
Learn's national cloud page says GCC
uses the worldwide Graph endpoint,

10
00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.060
so the environment is Global.
